{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794317151692,"sessionID":"ses_e3a6af12cffemPwVWkj0znar6y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_rrG2Gq6uGhY5fSAAb6jSb1vj","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"npm run lint","timeout":120000,"workdir":"/workspace/frontend"},"output":"\n> lint\n> eslint .\n\n\n/workspace/frontend/src/components/Dialog.tsx\n  13:3  error  Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\n/workspace/frontend/src/components/Dialog.tsx:13:3\n  11 |   const ref = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);\n  12 |   const closeRef = useRef(onClose);\n> 13 |   closeRef.current = onClose;\n     |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot update ref during render\n  14 |\n  15 |   useEffect(() => {\n  16 |     const previous = document.activeElement as HTMLElement | null;  react-hooks/refs\n\n✖ 1 problem (1 error, 0 warnings)\n\n","metadata":{"output":"\n> lint\n> eslint .\n\n\n/workspace/frontend/src/components/Dialog.tsx\n  13:3  error  Error: Cannot access refs during render\n\nReact refs are values that are not needed for rendering. Refs should only be accessed outside of render, such as in event handlers or effects. Accessing a ref value (the `current` property) during render can cause your component not to update as expected (https://react.dev/reference/react/useRef).\n\n/workspace/frontend/src/components/Dialog.tsx:13:3\n  11 |   const ref = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);\n  12 |   const closeRef = useRef(onClose);\n> 13 |   closeRef.current = onClose;\n     |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot update ref during render\n  14 |\n  15 |   useEffect(() => {\n  16 |     const previous = document.activeElement as HTMLElement | null;  react-hooks/refs\n\n✖ 1 problem (1 error, 0 warnin