{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794317334930,"sessionID":"ses_e3a6af12cffemPwVWkj0znar6y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_MPOKYZONjNrJtbuKXKk9C0ZV","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/backend/app.py\n@@\n import sqlite3\n+from contextlib import closing\n@@\n-    with sqlite3.connect(app.config[\"DATABASE\"]) as database:\n+    with closing(sqlite3.connect(app.config[\"DATABASE\"])) as database:\n*** Update File: /workspace/backend/tests/test_app.py\n@@\n import unittest\n+from contextlib import closing\n@@\n-from backend.app import PREVIEW_FIELDS, create_app\n+from backend.app import DIST, PREVIEW_FIELDS, create_app\n@@\n-        with sqlite3.connect(self.config[\"DATABASE\"]) as database:\n+        with closing(sqlite3.connect(self.config[\"DATABASE\"])) as database:\n@@\n-        with sqlite3.connect(self.config[\"DATABASE\"]) as database:\n+        with closing(sqlite3.connect(self.config[\"DATABASE\"])) as database, database:\n             database.execute(\"UPDATE tokens SET expires_at = '2000-01-01T00:00:00+00:00'\")\n@@\n     def test_request_size_is_bounded(self):\n@@\n         self.assertIn(\"error\", response.json)\n+\n+    @unittest.skipUnless((DIST / \"index.html\").is_file(), \"Build the frontend to test static serving.\")\n+    def test_production_frontend_and_assets_are_served(self):\n+        response = self.client.get(\"/\")\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 200)\n+        self.assertIn(b\"Marginal\", response.data)\n+        response.close()\n+        response = self.client.get(\"/illustration.svg\")\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 200)\n+        self.assertEqual(response.mimetype, \"image/svg+xml\")\n+        response.close()\n+        response = self.client.get(\"/a/frontend/route\")\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 200)\n+        response.close()\n*** Update File: /workspace/backend/tests/test_preview.py\n@@\n-        for value in (None, 1, \"\", \"example.com\", \"file:///tmp/file\", \"ftp://example.com\", \"https://\", \"http://example.com:0\", \"http://example.com:99999\", \"https://a:b@example.com\", \"https://example.com/\\n\", \"http://example.com\\\\@localhost\"):\n+        for value in (None, 1, \"\", \"example.com\", \"file:///tmp/file\", \"ftp://example.com\", \"https://\", \"http://example.com:0\", \"http://example.com:99999\", \"https://a:b@example.com\", \"https://example.com/a\\nb\", \"http://example.com\\\\@localhost\"):\n*** Update File: /workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx\n@@\n-            <div className=\"flex items-center gap-3 sm:gap-5\"><span className=\"flex items-center gap-2.5\"><span className=\"flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#e7ecde] font-serif text-sm text-olive\">{session.username.slice(0, 1).toUpperCase()}</span><span className=\"max-w-28 truncate text-xs font-medium sm:max-w-48\">{session.username}</span></span><span className=\"h-5 w-px bg-line\" /><button disabled={signingOut} onClick={() => void signOut()} className=\"flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md p-1 text-xs text-muted hover:text-ink disabled:opacity-50\">{signingOut ? <LoaderCircle size={14} className=\"animate-spin motion-reduce:animate-none\" /> : <LogOut size={14} />}<span className=\"hidden sm:inline\">Sign out</span></button></div>\n+            <div className=\"flex items-center gap-3 sm:gap-5\"><span className=\"flex items-center gap-2.5\"><span className=\"flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#e7ecde] font-serif text-sm text-olive\">{session.username.slice(0, 1).toUpperCase()}</span><span className=\"max-w-28 truncate text-xs font-medium sm:max-w-48\">{session.username}</span></span><span className=\"h-5 w-px bg-line\" /><button aria-label=\"Sign out\" disabled={signingOut} onClick={() => void signOut()} className=\"flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md p-1 text-xs text-muted hover:text-ink disabled:opacity-50\">{signingOut ? <LoaderCircle size={14} className=\"animate-spin motion-reduce:animate-none\" /> : <LogOut size={14} />}<span className=\"hidden sm:inline\">Sign out</span></button></div>\n*** Update File: /workspace/README.md\n@@\n-# App\n+# Marginal\n+\n+A private link library with automatically fetched page previews, persistent bearer-token accounts, and a React/Tailwind frontend.\n@@\n Dependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n+\n+## Local development\n+\n+```sh\n+python3 -m venv .venv\n+.venv/bin/pip install -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock\n+.venv/bin/gunicorn --bind 0.0.0.0:8000 --pythonpath backend app:app\n+```\n+\n+In another terminal, run `npm ci` and `npm run dev` from `frontend/`. Vite proxies `/api` to the backend. Run `npm run build` from `frontend/` to serve the production frontend from Flask instead.\n+\n+## Docker\n+\n+```sh\n+docker build -t marginal .\n+docker run --rm -p 8000:8000 -v \"$(pwd)/data:/app/data\" marginal\n+```\n+\n+SQLite is stored in `./data/bookmarks.sqlite3`. `DATA_DIR` can override the data directory. Accounts, previews, and login tokens survive server restarts. Passwords use scrypt hashes; opaque bearer tokens are stored only as SHA-256 hashes and expire after 30 days. Sign-out revokes the current token.\n+\n+## Checks\n+\n+```sh\n+.venv/bin/python -m unittest discover -s backend/tests -v\n+.venv/bin/pip install ruff\n+.venv/bin/ruff check backend\n+```\n+\n+From `frontend/`, run `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run build`. Backend tests use isolated temporary databases and a local HTTP fixture; no external network access is required. Building the frontend also enables the static-serving test.\n+\n+## API\n+\n+Register with `POST /api/auth/register` and log in with `POST /api/auth/login`, sending JSON `{\"username\":\"your-name\",\"password\":\"your-password\"}`. Login returns `{\"token\":\"…\"}`. Send `Authorization: Bearer <token>` on preview requests. `GET /api/auth/me` returns the current username; `POST /api/auth/logout` revokes the token.\n+\n+- `POST /api/previews`: JSON `{\"url\":\"https://example.com/\"}`; returns the saved preview with status 201.\n+- `GET /api/previews?page=1&page_size=12`: newest-created first; returns `items`, `total`, `page`, and `page_size`. Page sizes range from 1 to 100.\n+- `GET /api/previews/{id}`: one owned preview.\n+- `POST /api/previews/{id}/refresh`: refetches the original link without changing creation order.\n+- `DELETE /api/previews/{id}`: deletes the owned preview; returns 204.\n+\n+All API errors have a JSON `error` message. Another user's preview returns 404. Open Graph text takes precedence over standard metadata, relative image URLs resolve against the final page URL, and fetched text is stripped of markup. Pages without metadata are saved with empty text fields and a null image. HTML error pages retain their HTTP status code; unreachable and non-HTML pages produce an error without saving or replacing a preview.\n+\n+Fetching accepts only public HTTP(S) destinations, checks every redirect, pins connections to validated DNS addresses, and verifies HTTPS certificates. Private, loopback, reserved, and link-local addresses are blocked. Fetching is limited to five redirects, 2 MiB of HTML, and a 20-second transfer budget with per-socket timeouts. The sandbox has no general outbound network access, so live public link fetching requires a deployment with outbound access; the included tests exercise fetching through a local fixture.\n+\n+The signed-out frontend shows clearly labeled example previews. They are not saved records. Library search filters the current page, and grid/list views and paging work on your own saved links.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM backend/app.py\nM backend/tests/test_app.py\nM backend/tests/test_preview.py\nM frontend/src/App.tsx\nM README.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /workspace/backend/app.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/app.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/app.py\n@@ -1,8 +1,9 @@\n import hashlib\n import os\n import secrets\n import sqlite3\n+from contextlib import closing\n from datetime import UTC, datetime, timedelta\n from functools import wraps\n from pathlib import Path\n \n@@ -30,9 +31,9 @@\n     )\n     if test_config:\n         app.config.update(test_config)\n     Path(app.config[\"DATABASE\"]).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n-    with sqlite3.connect(app.config[\"DATABASE\"]) as database:\n+    with closing(sqlite3.connect(app.config[\"DATABASE\"])) as database:\n         database.executescript(\"\"\"\n             PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL;\n             PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n             CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS users (\n\nIndex: /workspace/backend/tests/test_app.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/tests/test_app.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/tests/test_app.py\n@@ -1,12 +1,13 @@\n import hashlib\n import sqlite3\n import tempfile\n import unittest\n+from contextlib import closing\n from pathlib import Path\n from unittest.mock import patch\n \n-from backend.app import PREVIEW_FIELDS, create_app\n+from backend.app import DIST, PREVIEW_FIELDS, create_app\n from backend.preview import PreviewError\n \n \n def fixture_preview(url=\"https://example.com/\", title=\"A good find\"):\n@@ -69,9 +70,9 @@\n             self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 401)\n         self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/auth/me\", headers=self.headers).json, {\"username\": \"alice\"})\n \n     def test_credentials_and_tokens_are_hashed(self):\n-        with sqlite3.connect(self.config[\"DATABASE\"]) as database:\n+        with closing(sqlite3.connect(self.config[\"DATABASE\"])) as database:\n             password_hash = database.execute(\"SELECT password_hash FROM users\").fetchone()[0]\n             token_hash = database.execute(\"SELECT token_hash FROM tokens\").fetchone()[0]\n         token = self.headers[\"Authorization\"].split()[1]\n         self.assertNotEqual(password_hash, \"secret\")\n@@ -154,16 +155,30 @@\n         self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/auth/logout\", headers=self.headers).status_code, 204)\n         self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/previews\", headers=self.headers).status_code, 401)\n \n     def test_expired_token_is_rejected(self):\n-        with sqlite3.connect(self.config[\"DATABASE\"]) as database:\n+        with closing(sqlite3.connect(self.config[\"DATABASE\"])) as database, database:\n             database.execute(\"UPDATE tokens SET expires_at = '2000-01-01T00:00:00+00:00'\")\n         self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/previews\", headers=self.headers).status_code, 401)\n \n     def test_request_size_is_bounded(self):\n         response = self.client.post(\"/api/previews\", json={\"url\": \"x\" * 20000}, headers=self.headers)\n         self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 413)\n         self.assertIn(\"error\", response.json)\n \n+    @unittest.skipUnless((DIST / \"index.html\").is_file(), \"Build the frontend to test static serving.\")\n+    def test_production_frontend_and_assets_are_served(self):\n+        response = self.client.get(\"/\")\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 200)\n+        self.assertIn(b\"Marginal\", response.data)\n+        response.close()\n+        response = self.client.get(\"/illustration.svg\")\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 200)\n+        self.assertEqual(response.mimetype, \"image/svg+xml\")\n+        response.close()\n+        response = self.client.get(\"/a/frontend/route\")\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 200)\n+        response.close()\n \n+\n if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n     unittest.main()\n\nIndex: /workspace/backend/tests/test_preview.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/tests/test_preview.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/tests/test_preview.py\n@@ -57,9 +57,9 @@\n \n \n class UrlSafetyTests(unittest.TestCase):\n     def test_invalid_urls(self):\n-        for value in (None, 1, \"\", \"example.com\", \"file:///tmp/file\", \"ftp://example.com\", \"https://\", \"http://example.com:0\", \"http://example.com:99999\", \"https://a:b@example.com\", \"https://example.com/\\n\", \"http://example.com\\\\@localhost\"):\n+        for value in (None, 1, \"\", \"example.com\", \"file:///tmp/file\", \"ftp://example.com\", \"https://\", \"http://example.com:0\", \"http://example.com:99999\", \"https://a:b@example.com\", \"https://example.com/a\\nb\", \"http://example.com\\\\@localhost\"):\n             with self.subTest(value=value), self.assertRaises(PreviewError):\n                 validated_url(value)\n \n     def test_unicode_url_is_encoded(self):\n\nIndex: /workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx\n+++ /workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx\n@@ -130,9 +130,9 @@\n <div className=\"lg:ml-[244px]\">\n   <header className=\"flex h-[83px] items-center justify-between gap-4 border-b border-line px-5 sm:px-9 xl:px-12\">\n     <div className=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><button aria-label=\"Open menu\" onClick={() => setMobileNav(true)} className=\"rounded-lg p-1.5 text-muted lg:hidden\"><Menu size={20} /></button><span className=\"font-serif text-2xl tracking-tight lg:hidden\">marginal.</span><span className=\"hidden items-center gap-2 text-[11px] text-muted lg:flex\"><Bookmark size={13} strokeWidth={1.5} />Your personal link library</span></div>\n     {restoring ? <span role=\"status\" className=\"flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-muted\"><LoaderCircle size={15} className=\"animate-spin motion-reduce:animate-none\" />Opening your library…</span> : session ? (\n-      <div className=\"flex items-center gap-3 sm:gap-5\"><span className=\"flex items-center gap-2.5\"><span className=\"flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#e7ecde] font-serif text-sm text-olive\">{session.username.slice(0, 1).toUpperCase()}</span><span className=\"max-w-28 truncate text-xs font-medium sm:max-w-48\">{session.username}</span></span><span className=\"h-5 w-px bg-line\" /><button disabled={signingOut} onClick={() => void signOut()} className=\"flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md p-1 text-xs text-muted hover:text-ink disabled:opacity-50\">{signingOut ? <LoaderCircle size={14} className=\"animate-spin motion-reduce:animate-none\" /> : <LogOut size={14} />}<span className=\"hidden sm:inline\">Sign out</span></button></div>\n+      <div className=\"flex items-center gap-3 sm:gap-5\"><span className=\"flex items-center gap-2.5\"><span className=\"flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#e7ecde] font-serif text-sm text-olive\">{session.username.slice(0, 1).toUpperCase()}</span><span className=\"max-w-28 truncate text-xs font-medium sm:max-w-48\">{session.username}</span></span><span className=\"h-5 w-px bg-line\" /><button aria-label=\"Sign out\" disabled={signingOut} onClick={() => void signOut()} className=\"flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md p-1 text-xs text-muted hover:text-ink disabled:opacity-50\">{signingOut ? <LoaderCircle size={14} className=\"animate-spin motion-reduce:animate-none\" /> : <LogOut size={14} />}<span className=\"hidden sm:inline\">Sign out</span></button></div>\n     ) : (\n       <div className=\"flex items-center gap-4 sm:gap-6\"><button onClick={() => setAuthMode(\"login\")} className=\"rounded text-xs text-muted hover:text-ink\">Sign in</button><button onClick={() => setAuthMode(\"register\")} className=\"flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg bg-olive px-3.5 py-2.5 text-xs font-medium text-white transition hover:bg-olive/90\">Make it yours<ArrowRight size={14} className=\"hidden sm:block\" /></button></div>\n     )}\n   </header>\n\nIndex: /workspace/README.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/README.md\n+++ /workspace/README.md\n@@ -1,6 +1,8 @@\n-# App\n+# Marginal\n \n+A private link library with automatically fetched page previews, persistent bearer-token accounts, and a React/Tailwind frontend.\n+\n ## Run contract\n \n - The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n - The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n@@ -12,4 +14,49 @@\n - `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n - `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n \n Dependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n+\n+## Local development\n+\n+```sh\n+python3 -m venv .venv\n+.venv/bin/pip install -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock\n+.venv/bin/gunicorn --bind 0.0.0.0:8000 --pythonpath backend app:app\n+```\n+\n+In another terminal, run `npm ci` and `npm run dev` from `frontend/`. Vite proxies `/api` to the backend. Run `npm run build` from `frontend/` to serve the production frontend from Flask instead.\n+\n+## Docker\n+\n+```sh\n+docker build -t marginal .\n+docker run --rm -p 8000:8000 -v \"$(pwd)/data:/app/data\" marginal\n+```\n+\n+SQLite is stored in `./data/bookmarks.sqlite3`. `DATA_DIR` can override the data directory. Accounts, previews, and login tokens survive server restarts. Passwords use scrypt hashes; opaque bearer tokens are stored only as SHA-256 hashes and expire after 30 days. Sign-out revokes the current token.\n+\n+## Checks\n+\n+```sh\n+.venv/bin/python -m unittest discover -s backend/tests -v\n+.venv/bin/pip install ruff\n+.venv/bin/ruff check backend\n+```\n+\n+From `frontend/`, run `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run build`. Backend tests use isolated temporary databases and a local HTTP fixture; no external network access is required. Building the frontend also enables the static-serving test.\n+\n+## API\n+\n+Register with `POST /api/auth/register` and log in with `POST /api/auth/login`, sending JSON `{\"username\":\"your-name\",\"password\":\"your-password\"}`. Login returns `{\"token\":\"…\"}`. Send `Authorization: Bearer <token>` on preview requests. `GET /api/auth/me` returns the current username; `POST /api/auth/logout` revokes the token.\n+\n+- `POST /api/previews`: JSON `{\"url\":\"https://example.com/\"}`; returns the saved preview with status 201.\n+- `GET /api/previews?page=1&page_size=12`: newest-created first; returns `items`, `total`, `page`, and `page_size`. Page sizes range from 1 to 100.\n+- `GET /api/previews/{id}`: one owned preview.\n+- `POST /api/previews/{id}/refresh`: refetches the original link without changing creation order.\n+- `DELETE /api/previews/{id}`: deletes the owned preview; returns 204.\n+\n+All API errors have a JSON `error` message. Another user's preview returns 404. Open Graph text takes precedence over standard metadata, relative image URLs resolve against the final page URL, and fetched text is stripped of markup. Pages without metadata are saved with empty text fields and a null image. HTML error pages retain their HTTP status code; unreachable and non-HTML pages produce an error without saving or replacing a preview.\n+\n+Fetching accepts only public HTTP(S) destinations, checks every redirect, pins connections to validated DNS addresses, and verifies HTTPS certificates. Private, loopback, reserved, and link-local addresses are blocked. Fetching is limited to five redirects, 2 MiB of HTML, and a 20-second transfer budget with per-socket timeouts. The sandbox has no general outbound network access, so live public link fetching requires a deployment with outbound access; the included tests exercise fetching through a local fixture.\n+\n+The signed-out frontend shows clearly labeled example previews. They are not saved records. Library search filters the current page, and grid/list views and paging work on your own saved links.\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/workspace/backend/app.py","relativePath":"backend/app.py","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/backend/app.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/app.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/app.py\n@@ -1,8 +1,9 @@\n import hashlib\n import os\n import secrets\n import sqlite3\n+from contextlib import closing\n from datetime import UTC, datetime, timedelta\n from functools import wraps\n from pathlib import Path\n \n@@ -30,9 +31,9 @@\n     )\n     if test_config:\n         app.config.update(test_config)\n     Path(app.config[\"DATABASE\"]).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n-    with sqlite3.connect(app.config[\"DATABASE\"]) as database:\n+    with closing(sqlite3.connect(app.config[\"DATABASE\"])) as database:\n         database.executescript(\"\"\"\n             PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL;\n             PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n             CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS users (\n","additions":2,"deletions":1},{"filePath":"/workspace/backend/tests/test_app.py","relativePath":"backend/tests/test_app.py","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/backend/tests/test_app.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/tests/test_app.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/tests/test_app.py\n@@ -1,12 +1,13 @@\n import hashlib\n import sqlite3\n import tempfile\n import unittest\n+from contextlib import closing\n from pathlib import Path\n from unittest.mock import patch\n \n-from backend.app import PREVIEW_FIELDS, create_app\n+from backend.app import DIST, PREVIEW_FIELDS, create_app\n from backend.preview import PreviewError\n \n \n def fixture_preview(url=\"https://example.com/\", title=\"A good find\"):\n@@ -69,9 +70,9 @@\n             self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 401)\n         self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/auth/me\", headers=self.headers).json, {\"username\": \"alice\"})\n \n     def test_credentials_and_tokens_are_hashed(self):\n-        with sqlite3.connect(self.config[\"DATABASE\"]) as database:\n+        with closing(sqlite3.connect(self.config[\"DATABASE\"])) as database:\n             password_hash = database.execute(\"SELECT password_hash FROM users\").fetchone()[0]\n             token_hash = database.execute(\"SELECT token_hash FROM tokens\").fetchone()[0]\n         token = self.headers[\"Authorization\"].split()[1]\n         self.assertNotEqual(password_hash, \"secret\")\n@@ -154,16 +155,30 @@\n         self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/auth/logout\", headers=self.headers).status_code, 204)\n         self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/previews\", headers=self.headers).status_code, 401)\n \n     def test_expired_token_is_rejected(self):\n-        with sqlite3.connect(self.config[\"DATABASE\"]) as database:\n+        with closing(sqlite3.connect(self.config[\"DATABASE\"])) as database, database:\n             database.execute(\"UPDATE tokens SET expires_at = '2000-01-01T00:00:00+00:00'\")\n         self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/previews\", headers=self.headers).status_code, 401)\n \n     def test_request_size_is_bounded(self):\n         response = self.client.post(\"/api/previews\", json={\"url\": \"x\" * 20000}, headers=self.headers)\n         self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 413)\n         self.assertIn(\"error\", response.json)\n \n+    @unittest.skipUnless((DIST / \"index.html\").is_file(), \"Build the frontend to test static serving.\")\n+    def test_production_frontend_and_assets_are_served(self):\n+        response = self.client.get(\"/\")\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 200)\n+        self.assertIn(b\"Marginal\", response.data)\n+        response.close()\n+        response = self.client.get(\"/illustration.svg\")\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 200)\n+        self.assertEqual(response.mimetype, \"image/svg+xml\")\n+        response.close()\n+        response = self.client.get(\"/a/frontend/route\")\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 200)\n+        response.close()\n \n+\n if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n     unittest.main()\n","additions":18,"deletions":3},{"filePath":"/workspace/backend/tests/test_preview.py","relativePath":"backend/tests/test_preview.py","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/backend/tests/test_preview.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/tests/test_preview.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/tests/test_preview.py\n@@ -57,9 +57,9 @@\n \n \n class UrlSafetyTests(unittest.TestCase):\n     def test_invalid_urls(self):\n-        for value in (None, 1, \"\", \"example.com\", \"file:///tmp/file\", \"ftp://example.com\", \"https://\", \"http://example.com:0\", \"http://example.com:99999\", \"https://a:b@example.com\", \"https://example.com/\\n\", \"http://example.com\\\\@localhost\"):\n+        for value in (None, 1, \"\", \"example.com\", \"file:///tmp/file\", \"ftp://example.com\", \"https://\", \"http://example.com:0\", \"http://example.com:99999\", \"https://a:b@example.com\", \"https://example.com/a\\nb\", \"http://example.com\\\\@localhost\"):\n             with self.subTest(value=value), self.assertRaises(PreviewError):\n                 validated_url(value)\n \n     def test_unicode_url_is_encoded(self):\n","additions":1,"deletions":1},{"filePath":"/workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx","relativePath":"frontend/src/App.tsx","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx\n+++ /workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx\n@@ -130,9 +130,9 @@\n <div className=\"lg:ml-[244px]\">\n   <header className=\"flex h-[83px] items-center justify-between gap-4 border-b border-line px-5 sm:px-9 xl:px-12\">\n     <div className=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><button aria-label=\"Open menu\" onClick={() => setMobileNav(true)} className=\"rounded-lg p-1.5 text-muted lg:hidden\"><Menu size={20} /></button><span className=\"font-serif text-2xl tracking-tight lg:hidden\">marginal.</span><span className=\"hidden items-center gap-2 text-[11px] text-muted lg:flex\"><Bookmark size={13} strokeWidth={1.5} />Your personal link library</span></div>\n     {restoring ? <span role=\"status\" className=\"flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-muted\"><LoaderCircle size={15} className=\"animate-spin motion-reduce:animate-none\" />Opening your library…</span> : session ? (\n-      <div className=\"flex items-center gap-3 sm:gap-5\"><span className=\"flex items-center gap-2.5\"><span className=\"flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#e7ecde] font-serif text-sm text-olive\">{session.username.slice(0, 1).toUpperCase()}</span><span className=\"max-w-28 truncate text-xs font-medium sm:max-w-48\">{session.username}</span></span><span className=\"h-5 w-px bg-line\" /><button disabled={signingOut} onClick={() => void signOut()} className=\"flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md p-1 text-xs text-muted hover:text-ink disabled:opacity-50\">{signingOut ? <LoaderCircle size={14} className=\"animate-spin motion-reduce:animate-none\" /> : <LogOut size={14} />}<span className=\"hidden sm:inline\">Sign out</span></button></div>\n+      <div className=\"flex items-center gap-3 sm:gap-5\"><span className=\"flex items-center gap-2.5\"><span className=\"flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#e7ecde] font-serif text-sm text-olive\">{session.username.slice(0, 1).toUpperCase()}</span><span className=\"max-w-28 truncate text-xs font-medium sm:max-w-48\">{session.username}</span></span><span className=\"h-5 w-px bg-line\" /><button aria-label=\"Sign out\" disabled={signingOut} onClick={() => void signOut()} className=\"flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md p-1 text-xs text-muted hover:text-ink disabled:opacity-50\">{signingOut ? <LoaderCircle size={14} className=\"animate-spin motion-reduce:animate-none\" /> : <LogOut size={14} />}<span className=\"hidden sm:inline\">Sign out</span></button></div>\n     ) : (\n       <div className=\"flex items-center gap-4 sm:gap-6\"><button onClick={() => setAuthMode(\"login\")} className=\"rounded text-xs text-muted hover:text-ink\">Sign in</button><button onClick={() => setAuthMode(\"register\")} className=\"flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg bg-olive px-3.5 py-2.5 text-xs font-medium text-white transition hover:bg-olive/90\">Make it yours<ArrowRight size={14} className=\"hidden sm:block\" /></button></div>\n     )}\n   </header>\n","additions":1,"deletions":1},{"filePath":"/workspace/README.md","relativePath":"README.md","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/README.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/README.md\n+++ /workspace/README.md\n@@ -1,6 +1,8 @@\n-# App\n+# Marginal\n \n+A private link library with automatically fetched page previews, persistent bearer-token accounts, and a React/Tailwind frontend.\n+\n ## Run contract\n \n - The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n - The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n@@ -12,4 +14,49 @@\n - `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n - `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n \n Dependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n+\n+## Local development\n+\n+```sh\n+python3 -m venv .venv\n+.venv/bin/pip install -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock\n+.venv/bin/gunicorn --bind 0.0.0.0:8000 --pythonpath backend app:app\n+```\n+\n+In another terminal, run `npm ci` and `npm run dev` from `frontend/`. Vite proxies `/api` to the backend. Run `npm run build` from `frontend/` to serve the production frontend from Flask instead.\n+\n+## Docker\n+\n+```sh\n+docker build -t marginal .\n+docker run --rm -p 8000:8000 -v \"$(pwd)/data:/app/data\" marginal\n+```\n+\n+SQLite is stored in `./data/bookmarks.sqlite3`. `DATA_DIR` can override the data directory. Accounts, previews, and login tokens survive server restarts. Passwords use scrypt hashes; opaque bearer tokens are stored only as SHA-256 hashes and expire after 30 days. Sign-out revokes the current token.\n+\n+## Checks\n+\n+```sh\n+.venv/bin/python -m unittest discover -s backend/tests -v\n+.venv/bin/pip install ruff\n+.venv/bin/ruff check backend\n+```\n+\n+From `frontend/`, run `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run build`. Backend tests use isolated temporary databases and a local HTTP fixture; no external network access is required. Building the frontend also enables the static-serving test.\n+\n+## API\n+\n+Register with `POST /api/auth/register` and log in with `POST /api/auth/login`, sending JSON `{\"username\":\"your-name\",\"password\":\"your-password\"}`. Login returns `{\"token\":\"…\"}`. Send `Authorization: Bearer <token>` on preview requests. `GET /api/auth/me` returns the current username; `POST /api/auth/logout` revokes the token.\n+\n+- `POST /api/previews`: JSON `{\"url\":\"https://example.com/\"}`; returns the saved preview with status 201.\n+- `GET /api/previews?page=1&page_size=12`: newest-created first; returns `items`, `total`, `page`, and `page_size`. Page sizes range from 1 to 100.\n+- `GET /api/previews/{id}`: one owned preview.\n+- `POST /api/previews/{id}/refresh`: refetches the original link without changing creation order.\n+- `DELETE /api/previews/{id}`: deletes the owned preview; returns 204.\n+\n+All API errors have a JSON `error` message. Another user's preview returns 404. Open Graph text takes precedence over standard metadata, relative image URLs resolve against the final page URL, and fetched text is stripped of markup. Pages without metadata are saved with empty text fields and a null image. HTML error pages retain their HTTP status code; unreachable and non-HTML pages produce an error without saving or replacing a preview.\n+\n+Fetching accepts only public HTTP(S) destinations, checks every redirect, pins connections to validated DNS addresses, and verifies HTTPS certificates. Private, loopback, reserved, and link-local addresses are blocked. Fetching is limited to five redirects, 2 MiB of HTML, and a 20-second transfer budget with per-socket timeouts. The sandbox has no general outbound network access, so live public link fetching requires a deployment with outbound access; the included tests exercise fetching through a local fixture.\n+\n+The signed-out frontend shows clearly labeled example previews. They are not saved records. Library search filters the current page, and grid/list views and paging work on your own saved links.\n","additions":48,"deletions":1}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM backend/app.py\nM backend/tests/test_app.py\nM backend/tests/test_preview.py\nM frontend/src/App.tsx\nM README.md","time":{"start":1794317334878,"end":1794317334902}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.encrypted","data":"gAAAAABq8xv8Y-0OA0-UM3R0NOK9EpzhMXWnRtAvO6Vzp-KY82tx_GnbODMVlcKIm0W5Arl069OwJsliatPDgusKSr9HGKb7ZCw6g4xDnLRlNTRcCAkqUHmZG_iieJVa7-4ZLg33BNvGTlGTd08JqHI2jvjwIb_Nl98MptltOHdO_w2U0EcOhsJi8idQvJ4QK0-URrMzXQKt70W